      "book": "Proverbs",
      "chapter": 1,
      "verse": 23,
      "startVerse": 23,
      "endVerse": 27,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "A lot of mess can be avoided if we just took the time to seek out wisdom. Solomon says that Wisdom is a person. As we progress through these chapters, we become wiser to the fact that wisdom is not found in anyone but the Lord. Jesus Christ IS wisdom. As we read and we see wisdom (though it's attributed to a woman for this specific viewpoint), we will see that Christ embodies every trait that Solomon gives to it. Including the trait of laughing at the pains of those that reject wisdom. Wisdom is giving them a chance to avoid destruction and pain and sorrow, and they have chosen to reject it. What other choice does wisdom have but to laugh at their pain, seeing as they chose to take it on themselves?",
