      "book": "Proverbs",
      "chapter": 2,
      "verse": 0,
      "startVerse": 0,
      "endVerse": 0,
      "author": "Tried By Fire",
      "authorHandle": "@TriedByFire",
      "text": "In the last chapter, we picked up this book with the understanding that Solomon was writing to the generation that was to follow him, specifically to his own children. He wanted to hand down wisdom to his kids so that they don’t make the same mistakes that he made, and so that they are properly prepared for the responsibilities in which God will (no doubt) give to them. These are things that we can personally take to heart as we learn and grow our own walks in the Lord. He tells us what to avoid and what to pay attention to. That will be the theme of this entire book, and he gives us application not just for friendships and simple understandings, but for marriages, how to treat enemies, what to look for when you are seeking knowledge and understanding, and how to avoid useless and vain conversations.",
      "likes": 0,
